### Independent-source comparison and identity resolution

- Anthropic's official Opus announcement history lists Claude Opus 5.5 (2026-09-22), Opus 5 (2026-07-24), Opus 4.8 (2026-05-28), Opus 4.7 (2026-04-16) and Opus 4.6 (2026-02-05), with the pre-4.5 models (4.5, 4.1, 4) appearing only in the model lifecycle history — there is no Opus 4.4 entry, and the numbering skips 4.2–4.4 entirely ([Claude Opus page](https://www.anthropic.com/claude/opus)).
- Anthropic's lifecycle table lists every current and recently retired Opus model with its status and retirement date; the Opus entries are `claude-opus-4-1-20250805`, `claude-opus-20250514`, `claude-3-opus-20240229` and `claude-2.x`. No 4.4 model was ever announced, deprecated or retired ([model deprecations](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations)).
- Anthropic's model-ID documentation and current models overview contain no `opus-4-4` string; the documented point-release convention is hyphenated (`claude-opus-4-5-20251101`, `claude-opus-5-5`) with no 4-4 example ([model IDs and versioning](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/model-ids-and-versions), [models overview](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/overview)).
- Live independent catalogs agree with the first-party record: OpenRouter exposes `anthropic/claude-opus-4.1`, `-4.5`, `-4.6`, `-4.7`, `-4.8` and the Opus 5/5.5 entries but no 4.4 ([OpenRouter models API](https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models)); models.dev's provider catalog contains `claude-opus-4`, `claude-opus-4-1`, `claude-opus-4-5`, `claude-opus-4-6`, `claude-opus-4-7` and `claude-opus-4-8` but no exact 4.4 ID ([models.dev API](https://models.dev/api.json)); OpenCode Zen's live catalog contains `claude-opus-4-5`, `-4-6`, `-4-7`, `-4-8`, `claude-opus-5` and `claude-opus-5-5` but no `claude-opus-4-4` ([OpenCode Zen models](https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models)); Vercel AI Gateway's model list contains no `claude-opus-4.4`/`claude-opus-4-4` entry ([Vercel AI Gateway models](https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/models)).
- Tracker lookups are empty as well: BenchLM's model page for `claude-opus-4-4` returns HTTP 404 ([BenchLM](https://benchlm.ai/models/claude-opus-4-4)), and the Hugging Face model search for `claude-opus-4.4` returns an empty result set ([Hugging Face API](https://huggingface.co/api/models?search=claude-opus-4.4&limit=50)). No Artificial Analysis, LLM Stats, Design Arena or Vals AI entry for Opus 4.4 was found.
- Multiple exact-phrase searches ("Claude Opus 4.4" with release/pricing/benchmark/API/model-card qualifiers, and the `opus-4-4` / `opus 4.4` spellings) surfaced only generic Claude pages and the real Opus 4.5/4.6/4.7/4.8/5/5.5 records — no exact 4.4 model card, system card, announcement, benchmark, or review.
- The conflict is therefore between the repository label and the public vendor record, not between vendors: the likely explanations are an interpolated label for Opus 4.5 or 4.6, an internal/preview codename, or a phantom entry.
- Because no exact model or benchmark was verified, Opus 4.5/4.6/4.8 measurements were deliberately not merged into this record. No normalized score is defensible without evidence for the exact ID.

